[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186118059 :answer-field/choices 17592186118064] [:db/retract 17592186118059 :answer-field/choices 17592186118060] [:db/retract 17592186118059 :answer-field/choices 17592186118061] [:db/retract 17592186118059 :answer-field/choices 17592186118062] [:db/retract 17592186118059 :answer-field/choices 17592186118063] {:db/id 17592186119923 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" "question-34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" :question/id #uuid "de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" :question/math-academy-id "q-75636" :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]=-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=-3{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-3{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 3{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8df14e3b-06f0-5de6-a3f3-c95b09e3bf3f" "answer-0a561db8-da05-5488-90b2-b1499bdfd024" "answer-68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d" "answer-14137556-54c3-5d40-a07b-5a7c1bb6e3a5" "answer-62097d8f-b2fe-5ff4-a7b0-e3bbc5636bd0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8df14e3b-06f0-5de6-a3f3-c95b09e3bf3f" :answer/id #uuid "8df14e3b-06f0-5de6-a3f3-c95b09e3bf3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a561db8-da05-5488-90b2-b1499bdfd024" :answer/id #uuid "0a561db8-da05-5488-90b2-b1499bdfd024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d" :answer/id #uuid "68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14137556-54c3-5d40-a07b-5a7c1bb6e3a5" :answer/id #uuid "14137556-54c3-5d40-a07b-5a7c1bb6e3a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62097d8f-b2fe-5ff4-a7b0-e3bbc5636bd0" :answer/id #uuid "62097d8f-b2fe-5ff4-a7b0-e3bbc5636bd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120320 :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]=-4[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=-4{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}-4{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118059 :answer-field/correct "answer-d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e97f2413-80bb-5bcf-bb04-ab19ba48bdaa" "answer-d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2" "answer-a4632e22-167c-5056-9f27-8ad30a2dcc0f" "answer-02117761-522d-518e-9380-cd3df0b411cd" "answer-8680a3ba-b8c5-5a4d-bba9-8c97bc9e294a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e97f2413-80bb-5bcf-bb04-ab19ba48bdaa" :answer/id #uuid "e97f2413-80bb-5bcf-bb04-ab19ba48bdaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2" :answer/id #uuid "d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4632e22-167c-5056-9f27-8ad30a2dcc0f" :answer/id #uuid "a4632e22-167c-5056-9f27-8ad30a2dcc0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02117761-522d-518e-9380-cd3df0b411cd" :answer/id #uuid "02117761-522d-518e-9380-cd3df0b411cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8680a3ba-b8c5-5a4d-bba9-8c97bc9e294a" :answer/id #uuid "8680a3ba-b8c5-5a4d-bba9-8c97bc9e294a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369" :question/id #uuid "34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369" :question/math-academy-id "q-75642" :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=2[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=2{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-2{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/id #uuid "d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35f96482-abb5-57cb-8ffa-3db8da48fb19" "answer-04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9" "answer-2cc05134-02b1-5727-8502-07a1f3d7d9e6" "answer-19a0357a-ce57-58ed-bfb1-8181d4484baa" "answer-de9cfaf8-1939-5e03-9914-e2205bc5fb25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35f96482-abb5-57cb-8ffa-3db8da48fb19" :answer/id #uuid "35f96482-abb5-57cb-8ffa-3db8da48fb19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9" :answer/id #uuid "04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cc05134-02b1-5727-8502-07a1f3d7d9e6" :answer/id #uuid "2cc05134-02b1-5727-8502-07a1f3d7d9e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19a0357a-ce57-58ed-bfb1-8181d4484baa" :answer/id #uuid "19a0357a-ce57-58ed-bfb1-8181d4484baa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de9cfaf8-1939-5e03-9914-e2205bc5fb25" :answer/id #uuid "de9cfaf8-1939-5e03-9914-e2205bc5fb25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881" :question/id #uuid "848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881" :question/math-academy-id "q-157254" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $3{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}=0.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2} & =3[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/id #uuid "e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0248fac4-7021-5d3c-8fe6-630d74a3d1b5" "answer-de17d5bf-c3c6-5996-a382-6447bcc6e98a" "answer-e5988f07-d1dc-55e6-8850-b106bbc457fe" "answer-a19b5317-af1f-54a5-aa91-38cce6394e14" "answer-2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0248fac4-7021-5d3c-8fe6-630d74a3d1b5" :answer/id #uuid "0248fac4-7021-5d3c-8fe6-630d74a3d1b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de17d5bf-c3c6-5996-a382-6447bcc6e98a" :answer/id #uuid "de17d5bf-c3c6-5996-a382-6447bcc6e98a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5988f07-d1dc-55e6-8850-b106bbc457fe" :answer/id #uuid "e5988f07-d1dc-55e6-8850-b106bbc457fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a19b5317-af1f-54a5-aa91-38cce6394e14" :answer/id #uuid "a19b5317-af1f-54a5-aa91-38cce6394e14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530" :answer/id #uuid "2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997" :question/id #uuid "5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997" :question/math-academy-id "q-105317" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 20 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nIII. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solution." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+20{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-13{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 20 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(0)+9(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0$, we get that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e608ec51-2291-5759-a881-171cd19404a6" "answer-2aa4ebb0-8d31-5131-bf0e-7bb725b939ee" "answer-09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2" "answer-3fe615b5-1980-5ec3-8f2a-a28dfe3cf0c6" "answer-466b980c-756d-5db4-8e7c-797a12ae9d1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e608ec51-2291-5759-a881-171cd19404a6" :answer/id #uuid "e608ec51-2291-5759-a881-171cd19404a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2aa4ebb0-8d31-5131-bf0e-7bb725b939ee" :answer/id #uuid "2aa4ebb0-8d31-5131-bf0e-7bb725b939ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2" :answer/id #uuid "09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fe615b5-1980-5ec3-8f2a-a28dfe3cf0c6" :answer/id #uuid "3fe615b5-1980-5ec3-8f2a-a28dfe3cf0c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-466b980c-756d-5db4-8e7c-797a12ae9d1a" :answer/id #uuid "466b980c-756d-5db4-8e7c-797a12ae9d1a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121122 :tutorial/content "We say that two vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$ are **linearly independent** if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\nx_1 \\mathbf{v}_1 + x_2 \\mathbf{v}_2 = \\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis $x_1 = x_2 = 0.$ Otherwise, if there exists any solution other than $x_1 = x_2 = 0,$ then we say that the two vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$ are **linearly dependent**.\n\nTo illustrate, let's consider two sets of vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/46/46c22d599752ded730a67bfd57b4dfe238e512f6dff2d561afaf2f145c8118c2.svg)\n\n- For the first set ${\\color{blue}(\\textrm{I})},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is true only if $x_1=x_2=0.$ So, the set $\\color{blue}(\\textrm{I})$ is *linearly independent*.\n\n- On the other hand, for the second set ${\\color{red}(\\textrm{II})},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation has solutions other than $x_1=x_2=0.$ For example, $x_1=2$ and $x_2=1$ gives\n![](images/14/145f500e491087587478f03bd52ae180a7b4237acf17db0317ca07d28f389c56.svg)\nTherefore, the set $\\color{red}(\\textrm{II})$ is *not* linearly independent. Rather, it is *linearly dependent*.\n\n**Note:** You may notice that the vectors in the set $\\color{red}(\\textrm{II})$ were parallel (i.e. multiples of one another), while the vectors in set $\\color{blue}(\\textrm{I})$ were not. This trend holds in general, for all sets of two vectors:\n\n- a set of two vectors is *linearly dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel, while\n\n- a set of two vectors is *linearly independent* if and only if the two vectors are not parallel." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" :question/id #uuid "de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04"] ["question-de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" :question/math-academy-id "q-75636"] ["question-de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$"] ["question-de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]=-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=-3{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-3{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 3{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."] ["question-de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22"] ["answer-8df14e3b-06f0-5de6-a3f3-c95b09e3bf3f" :answer/id #uuid "8df14e3b-06f0-5de6-a3f3-c95b09e3bf3f"] ["answer-8df14e3b-06f0-5de6-a3f3-c95b09e3bf3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8df14e3b-06f0-5de6-a3f3-c95b09e3bf3f" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-0a561db8-da05-5488-90b2-b1499bdfd024" :answer/id #uuid "0a561db8-da05-5488-90b2-b1499bdfd024"] ["answer-0a561db8-da05-5488-90b2-b1499bdfd024" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0a561db8-da05-5488-90b2-b1499bdfd024" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d" :answer/id #uuid "68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d"] ["answer-68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-14137556-54c3-5d40-a07b-5a7c1bb6e3a5" :answer/id #uuid "14137556-54c3-5d40-a07b-5a7c1bb6e3a5"] ["answer-14137556-54c3-5d40-a07b-5a7c1bb6e3a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-14137556-54c3-5d40-a07b-5a7c1bb6e3a5" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-62097d8f-b2fe-5ff4-a7b0-e3bbc5636bd0" :answer/id #uuid "62097d8f-b2fe-5ff4-a7b0-e3bbc5636bd0"] ["answer-62097d8f-b2fe-5ff4-a7b0-e3bbc5636bd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-62097d8f-b2fe-5ff4-a7b0-e3bbc5636bd0" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/correct "answer-68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d"] ["answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/choices "answer-8df14e3b-06f0-5de6-a3f3-c95b09e3bf3f"] ["answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/choices "answer-0a561db8-da05-5488-90b2-b1499bdfd024"] ["answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/choices "answer-68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d"] ["answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/choices "answer-14137556-54c3-5d40-a07b-5a7c1bb6e3a5"] ["answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/choices "answer-62097d8f-b2fe-5ff4-a7b0-e3bbc5636bd0"] ["question-de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22"] [17592186119923 :knowledge-point/questions "question-de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04"] [17592186120320 :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]?$"] [17592186120320 :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]=-4[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=-4{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}-4{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."] [17592186120320 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-e97f2413-80bb-5bcf-bb04-ab19ba48bdaa" :answer/id #uuid "e97f2413-80bb-5bcf-bb04-ab19ba48bdaa"] ["answer-e97f2413-80bb-5bcf-bb04-ab19ba48bdaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e97f2413-80bb-5bcf-bb04-ab19ba48bdaa" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2" :answer/id #uuid "d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2"] ["answer-d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-a4632e22-167c-5056-9f27-8ad30a2dcc0f" :answer/id #uuid "a4632e22-167c-5056-9f27-8ad30a2dcc0f"] ["answer-a4632e22-167c-5056-9f27-8ad30a2dcc0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a4632e22-167c-5056-9f27-8ad30a2dcc0f" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-02117761-522d-518e-9380-cd3df0b411cd" :answer/id #uuid "02117761-522d-518e-9380-cd3df0b411cd"] ["answer-02117761-522d-518e-9380-cd3df0b411cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-02117761-522d-518e-9380-cd3df0b411cd" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-8680a3ba-b8c5-5a4d-bba9-8c97bc9e294a" :answer/id #uuid "8680a3ba-b8c5-5a4d-bba9-8c97bc9e294a"] ["answer-8680a3ba-b8c5-5a4d-bba9-8c97bc9e294a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8680a3ba-b8c5-5a4d-bba9-8c97bc9e294a" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]"] [17592186118059 :answer-field/correct "answer-d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2"] [17592186118059 :answer-field/choices "answer-e97f2413-80bb-5bcf-bb04-ab19ba48bdaa"] [17592186118059 :answer-field/choices "answer-d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2"] [17592186118059 :answer-field/choices "answer-a4632e22-167c-5056-9f27-8ad30a2dcc0f"] [17592186118059 :answer-field/choices "answer-02117761-522d-518e-9380-cd3df0b411cd"] [17592186118059 :answer-field/choices "answer-8680a3ba-b8c5-5a4d-bba9-8c97bc9e294a"] ["question-34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369" :question/id #uuid "34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369"] ["question-34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369" :question/math-academy-id "q-75642"] ["question-34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369" :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$"] ["question-34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=2[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=2{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-2{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."] ["question-34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/id #uuid "d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc"] ["answer-35f96482-abb5-57cb-8ffa-3db8da48fb19" :answer/id #uuid "35f96482-abb5-57cb-8ffa-3db8da48fb19"] ["answer-35f96482-abb5-57cb-8ffa-3db8da48fb19" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-35f96482-abb5-57cb-8ffa-3db8da48fb19" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9" :answer/id #uuid "04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9"] ["answer-04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-2cc05134-02b1-5727-8502-07a1f3d7d9e6" :answer/id #uuid "2cc05134-02b1-5727-8502-07a1f3d7d9e6"] ["answer-2cc05134-02b1-5727-8502-07a1f3d7d9e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2cc05134-02b1-5727-8502-07a1f3d7d9e6" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-19a0357a-ce57-58ed-bfb1-8181d4484baa" :answer/id #uuid "19a0357a-ce57-58ed-bfb1-8181d4484baa"] ["answer-19a0357a-ce57-58ed-bfb1-8181d4484baa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-19a0357a-ce57-58ed-bfb1-8181d4484baa" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-de9cfaf8-1939-5e03-9914-e2205bc5fb25" :answer/id #uuid "de9cfaf8-1939-5e03-9914-e2205bc5fb25"] ["answer-de9cfaf8-1939-5e03-9914-e2205bc5fb25" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-de9cfaf8-1939-5e03-9914-e2205bc5fb25" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/correct "answer-04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9"] ["answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/choices "answer-35f96482-abb5-57cb-8ffa-3db8da48fb19"] ["answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/choices "answer-04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9"] ["answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/choices "answer-2cc05134-02b1-5727-8502-07a1f3d7d9e6"] ["answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/choices "answer-19a0357a-ce57-58ed-bfb1-8181d4484baa"] ["answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/choices "answer-de9cfaf8-1939-5e03-9914-e2205bc5fb25"] ["question-34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc"] [17592186119923 :knowledge-point/questions "question-34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369"] ["question-848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881" :question/id #uuid "848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881"] ["question-848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881" :question/math-academy-id "q-157254"] ["question-848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $3{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}=0.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent."] ["question-848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2} & =3[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""] ["question-848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/id #uuid "e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d"] ["answer-0248fac4-7021-5d3c-8fe6-630d74a3d1b5" :answer/id #uuid "0248fac4-7021-5d3c-8fe6-630d74a3d1b5"] ["answer-0248fac4-7021-5d3c-8fe6-630d74a3d1b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-0248fac4-7021-5d3c-8fe6-630d74a3d1b5" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-de17d5bf-c3c6-5996-a382-6447bcc6e98a" :answer/id #uuid "de17d5bf-c3c6-5996-a382-6447bcc6e98a"] ["answer-de17d5bf-c3c6-5996-a382-6447bcc6e98a" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-de17d5bf-c3c6-5996-a382-6447bcc6e98a" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-e5988f07-d1dc-55e6-8850-b106bbc457fe" :answer/id #uuid "e5988f07-d1dc-55e6-8850-b106bbc457fe"] ["answer-e5988f07-d1dc-55e6-8850-b106bbc457fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-e5988f07-d1dc-55e6-8850-b106bbc457fe" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-a19b5317-af1f-54a5-aa91-38cce6394e14" :answer/id #uuid "a19b5317-af1f-54a5-aa91-38cce6394e14"] ["answer-a19b5317-af1f-54a5-aa91-38cce6394e14" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a19b5317-af1f-54a5-aa91-38cce6394e14" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530" :answer/id #uuid "2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530"] ["answer-2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/correct "answer-2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530"] ["answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/choices "answer-0248fac4-7021-5d3c-8fe6-630d74a3d1b5"] ["answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/choices "answer-de17d5bf-c3c6-5996-a382-6447bcc6e98a"] ["answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/choices "answer-e5988f07-d1dc-55e6-8850-b106bbc457fe"] ["answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/choices "answer-a19b5317-af1f-54a5-aa91-38cce6394e14"] ["answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/choices "answer-2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530"] ["question-848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d"] [17592186119924 :knowledge-point/questions "question-848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881"] ["question-5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997" :question/id #uuid "5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997"] ["question-5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997" :question/math-academy-id "q-105317"] ["question-5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 20 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nIII. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solution."] ["question-5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997" :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+20{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-13{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 20 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(0)+9(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0$, we get that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true."] ["question-5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e"] ["answer-e608ec51-2291-5759-a881-171cd19404a6" :answer/id #uuid "e608ec51-2291-5759-a881-171cd19404a6"] ["answer-e608ec51-2291-5759-a881-171cd19404a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-e608ec51-2291-5759-a881-171cd19404a6" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-2aa4ebb0-8d31-5131-bf0e-7bb725b939ee" :answer/id #uuid "2aa4ebb0-8d31-5131-bf0e-7bb725b939ee"] ["answer-2aa4ebb0-8d31-5131-bf0e-7bb725b939ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2aa4ebb0-8d31-5131-bf0e-7bb725b939ee" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2" :answer/id #uuid "09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2"] ["answer-09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-3fe615b5-1980-5ec3-8f2a-a28dfe3cf0c6" :answer/id #uuid "3fe615b5-1980-5ec3-8f2a-a28dfe3cf0c6"] ["answer-3fe615b5-1980-5ec3-8f2a-a28dfe3cf0c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-3fe615b5-1980-5ec3-8f2a-a28dfe3cf0c6" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-466b980c-756d-5db4-8e7c-797a12ae9d1a" :answer/id #uuid "466b980c-756d-5db4-8e7c-797a12ae9d1a"] ["answer-466b980c-756d-5db4-8e7c-797a12ae9d1a" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-466b980c-756d-5db4-8e7c-797a12ae9d1a" :answer/value "None of the statements are true"] ["answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/correct "answer-09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2"] ["answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/choices "answer-e608ec51-2291-5759-a881-171cd19404a6"] ["answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/choices "answer-2aa4ebb0-8d31-5131-bf0e-7bb725b939ee"] ["answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/choices "answer-09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2"] ["answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/choices "answer-3fe615b5-1980-5ec3-8f2a-a28dfe3cf0c6"] ["answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/choices "answer-466b980c-756d-5db4-8e7c-797a12ae9d1a"] ["question-5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e"] [17592186119925 :knowledge-point/questions "question-5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997"] [17592186121122 :tutorial/content "We say that two vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$ are **linearly independent** if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\nx_1 \\mathbf{v}_1 + x_2 \\mathbf{v}_2 = \\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis $x_1 = x_2 = 0.$ Otherwise, if there exists any solution other than $x_1 = x_2 = 0,$ then we say that the two vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$ are **linearly dependent**.\n\nTo illustrate, let's consider two sets of vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/46/46c22d599752ded730a67bfd57b4dfe238e512f6dff2d561afaf2f145c8118c2.svg)\n\n- For the first set ${\\color{blue}(\\textrm{I})},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is true only if $x_1=x_2=0.$ So, the set $\\color{blue}(\\textrm{I})$ is *linearly independent*.\n\n- On the other hand, for the second set ${\\color{red}(\\textrm{II})},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation has solutions other than $x_1=x_2=0.$ For example, $x_1=2$ and $x_2=1$ gives\n![](images/14/145f500e491087587478f03bd52ae180a7b4237acf17db0317ca07d28f389c56.svg)\nTherefore, the set $\\color{red}(\\textrm{II})$ is *not* linearly independent. Rather, it is *linearly dependent*.\n\n**Note:** You may notice that the vectors in the set $\\color{red}(\\textrm{II})$ were parallel (i.e. multiples of one another), while the vectors in set $\\color{blue}(\\textrm{I})$ were not. This trend holds in general, for all sets of two vectors:\n\n- a set of two vectors is *linearly dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel, while\n\n- a set of two vectors is *linearly independent* if and only if the two vectors are not parallel."]] "retractions" [[17592186120320 :question/problem "The set ${a_{1}, a_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be $a_{2}$ if\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$?"] [17592186118059 :answer-field/choices 17592186118064] [17592186118059 :answer-field/choices 17592186118060] [17592186118059 :answer-field/choices 17592186118061] [17592186118059 :answer-field/choices 17592186118062] [17592186118059 :answer-field/choices 17592186118063] [17592186121122 :tutorial/content "We say that two vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$ are **linearly independent** if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\nx_1 \\mathbf{v}_1 + x_2 \\mathbf{v}_2 = \\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis $x_1 = x_2 = 0.$ Otherwise, if there exists any solution other than $x_1 = x_2 = 0,$ then we say that the two vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$ are **linearly dependent**.\n\nTo illustrate, let's consider two sets of vectors in $\\mathbb{R}^2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/46/46c22d599752ded730a67bfd57b4dfe238e512f6dff2d561afaf2f145c8118c2.svg)\n\n- For the first set ${\\color{blue}(\\textrm{I})},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is true only if $x_1=x_2=0.$ So, the set $\\color{blue}(\\textrm{I})$ is *linearly independent*.\n\n- On the other hand, for the second set ${\\color{red}(\\textrm{II})},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above equation has solutions other than $x_1=x_2=0.$ For example, $x_1=2$ and $x_2=1$ gives\n![](images/14/145f500e491087587478f03bd52ae180a7b4237acf17db0317ca07d28f389c56.svg)\nTherefore, the set $\\color{red}(\\textrm{II})$ is *not* linearly independent. Rather, it is *linearly dependent*.\n\n**Note:** You may notice that the vectors in the set $\\color{red}(\\textrm{II})$ were parallel (i.e. multiples of one another), while the vectors in set $\\color{blue}(\\textrm{I})$ were not. This trend holds in general, for all sets of two vectors:\n\n- a set of two vectors is *linearly dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel, while\n\n- a set of two vectors is *linearly independent* if and only if the two vectors are not parallel."]]}]